## Independent-review fix round 2

Closed the remaining zero-gross tolerance edge from `task-4-rereview.md` in
`core/strategy_policy/contracts_v3.py` only.

`PortfolioFeaturesV3` now applies structural emptiness before numeric tolerance:

- when gross exposure is exactly zero, both sector and industry exposure tuples must be empty;
- when gross exposure is positive, both tuples must be nonempty; and
- only positive-gross total reconciliation uses the canonical floating-point tolerance.

The bounded direct smoke passed for exact zero with empty tuples; rejection of `5e-13` sector or
industry exposure at zero gross; rejection of either empty tuple at positive gross; and intentional
acceptance/rejection immediately inside/outside the positive-gross tolerance. The disposable script
was removed. The 41 focused strategy-policy tests, Ruff, `py_compile`, and `git diff --check` also
passed; warnings remained limited to the existing websockets deprecation, sandbox-denied pytest
cache, and Windows line-ending notice.

